      "value": "you could incorporate it into avatars if you want this kinda early\n\nYou can set your eye track in behaviours to animation, then make a look/aim point on your eye bones on a specific point like a cube, then have something like your hand designate where the cube is, like on the camera lens, then world-pos lock the cube.\n\nif the eyetrack to animation doesnt work, you could just duplicate the eyes and switch the material to invis for the vrceyetrack eyes and the duplicate manual eyes.\n\ni havent tested the eyetrack to animation method, but in theory it would work, but only stationary cameras, the new dolly system obviously wouldn't work unless you want it only looking one direction.",
